    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498803/assistant-coach-track-parttime": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Track, Part-Time",
      "description": "Assistant Coach, Track, Part-Time Apply now Job no: 498803 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Women's Track and Field Position Type: Staff Part-Time Overview: This Individual will provide critical support to the NCAA Division I Track & Field program by assisting with day-to-day team operations, student-athlete development, and event execution. Working closely with the Head Coach and coaching staff, this role contributes to training sessions, administrative scheduling, practice setup, and home meet management while ensuring full compliance with all NCAA, conference, and institutional regulations. The ideal candidate brings competitive track and field experience, strong communication skills, and a flexible schedule to accommodate afternoon practices, weekend meets, and travel demands. Responsibilities: Coaching & Athlete Development Assist head and assistant coaches with designing and executing daily training, conditioning, and technical drill sessions. Provide real-time instructional feedback and performance breakdown to student-athletes during practice and competition. Support the implementation of event-specific injury prevention and athletic recovery protocols. Operations & Event Management Lead facility setup and teardown for daily practice sessions and all home competitive meets. Manage meet logistics, including timing system setup, official officiating coordination, and field event measurement support. Oversee team equipment, maintaining inventory, gear distribution, and standard safety inspections. Administration & Logistics Coordinate team travel arrangements, including meal orders, hotel rooming lists, and ground transportation. Maintain accurate operational records, such as practice attendance, workout tracking, and equipment logs. Assist in organizing video footage and technical analysis for post-meet review sessions. Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Required: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution (or an equivalent combination of education, athletic experience, and formal training). Required: Minimum of 1 to 2 years of competitive or coaching experience in track and field at the collegiate (NCAA/NAIA) or elite scholastic (high school/club) level. Must have hands-on experience in athletic training operations, practice setup, or sport-specific skill instruction. Knowledge: NCAA Rules & Compliance: Practical understanding of NCAA Division I rules, bylaws, and ethical standards surrounding student-athlete engagement and athletic operations. Track & Field Mechanics: In-depth knowledge of technical execution, training methodologies, and safety protocols across track and field event disciplines. Meet Operations & Logistics: Familiarity with home meet management, facility setup standards, and standard track and field timing/scoring software (e.g., Hy-Tek, FinishLynx, MeetPro). Skills: Instruction & Coaching: Ability to break down complex movement mechanics and deliver clear, actionable feedback to student-athletes. Organization & Time Management: Strong logistical skills to coordinate travel, equipment, facilities, and schedules under tight deadlines. Technical Proficiency: Competency with basic administrative software (Microsoft Office, Google Workspace) and video breakdown tools for performance analysis. Communication: Clear verbal and written communication skills for interacting with student-athletes, coaching staff, game officials, and athletic administration. Abilities: Adaptability & Flexibility: Ability to work irregular hours, including early mornings, evenings, weekends, and extended multi-day travel schedules. Physical Capability: Ability to stand for prolonged periods outdoors in varying weather conditions and lift/move heavy track equipment (e.g., hurdles, mats, throwing implements up to 50 lbs). Required: Valid Driver’s License with an acceptable driving record (required for team transport/van operation). First Aid, CPR, and AED certifications (or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire). NCAA Division I Coaches Certification / Recruiting Test clearance (must be completed annually upon hire prior to engaging in countable athletically related activities). Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 9, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498802/assistant-coach-golf-parttime": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Golf, Part-Time",
      "description": "Assistant Coach, Golf, Part-Time Apply now Job no: 498802 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Golf Position Type: Staff Part-Time Overview: This individual will support the Head Coach in building and sustaining a competitive NCAA Division I women's golf program. This position exists to enhance student-athlete skill development, assist with strategic course management and practice execution, and manage operational logistics while maintaining strict compliance with all NCAA, conference, and university regulations. Responsibilities: Coaching & Student-Athlete Development Assist the Head Coach in planning and executing daily practice sessions, short-game drills, and range work. Provide instruction on swing mechanics, course management, strategy, and mental preparation during practices and competitive rounds. Travel with the team to off-campus practices and tournament sites, providing on-course coaching and strategy support. Operations & Logistics Coordinate team travel arrangements, including vehicle reservations, lodging, meal planning, and tournament entry documentation. Assist with gear and uniform distribution, inventory tracking, and golf equipment maintenance. Help organize team schedules, facility access, and tee-time bookings with home and local golf courses. Recruiting & Administration Support the Head Coach in identifying, evaluating, and tracking prospective student-athletes within NCAA guidelines. Maintain administrative records, including practice logs, athlete schedules, and team communications. Assist in organizing home tournaments, junior clinics, or program fundraising initiatives as assigned. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Required: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Required: Minimum of 1 to 2 years of competitive playing or coaching experience at the collegiate (NCAA/NAIA) or elite amateur/junior golf level. Demonstrated knowledge of golf strategy, swing mechanics, and course management techniques. Knowledge: Golf Mechanics & Strategy: In-depth knowledge of swing fundamentals, short-game techniques, course management strategies, and mental game principles. NCAA Rules: Firm understanding of NCAA Division I bylaws regarding practice hours, recruiting restrictions, and student-athlete eligibility. Performance Technology: Familiarity with golf launch monitors (TrackMan, Quad), putting sensors, and statistical tracking platforms (e.g., Strokes Gained analysis). Skills: Instruction: Ability to effectively teach and communicate technical golf concepts to elite-level female student-athletes. Logistical Planning: Strong organizational skills to manage complex travel itineraries, tee times, budget tracking, and tournament schedules. Communication: Clear, professional verbal and written communication skills when engaging with athletes, recruits, parents, course staff, and university personnel. Abilities: Schedule Flexibility: Ability to travel extensively and work irregular hours, including early mornings, weekends, and multi-day tournament trips. Physical Requirement: Ability to walk 18+ holes of golf per day in varying outdoor weather conditions while carrying golf equipment or supplies up to 30 lbs. Driver Capability: Ability to safely transport student-athletes long distances in university passenger vans. Required: Valid Driver’s License with an acceptable driving record (required for team transport via department vans). First Aid, CPR, and AED certifications (or ability to obtain within 30 days of hire). NCAA Division I Coaches Certification / Recruiting Test clearance (must be passed annually upon hire). Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 8, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
