    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498779/assistant-director-club-sports-multimedia-marketing": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Club Sports Multimedia & Marketing",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Club Sports Multimedia & Marketing Apply now Job no: 498779 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Campus Recreation Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: Robert Morris University is proud to offer a safe and inclusive campus community where students, faculty, and staff can thrive and be unstoppable. Through a wide variety of programs, services, and amenities, students and employees are empowered to explore possibilities, develop passions, and master skills that will position them for success in both career and life. Robert Morris University Campus Recreation is seeking a strategic, creative, and highly motivated leader to serve as the Assistant Director of Club Sports Multimedia & Marketing. Reporting directly to the Campus Recreation leadership team, this position provides high-level administrative direction, operational oversight, and creative vision for the Club Sports department’s media landscape. The Assistant Director is responsible for directing comprehensive live broadcast productions, designing multi-platform digital marketing strategies, and spearheading program-wide student-athlete recruitment operations. By building collaborative partnerships across campus and establishing high-quality production standards, the Assistant Director plays a vital role in expanding the reach, visibility, and brand equity of RMU Club Sports. Responsibilities: Direct all game-day video production and live streaming operations for club sports competitions, podcasts, and department events, establishing high-quality broadcast benchmarks that meet or exceed collegiate league standards. Conceptualize, develop, and execute long-term branding and marketing strategies designed to maximize club sports visibility, drive spectator attendance, and increase community engagement. Oversee the creation of professional live stream graphics packages, including scorebugs, motion overlays, intermission screens, and real-time team statistics, to deliver an industry-standard broadcast experience. Recruit, hire, train, schedule, and formally evaluate a dedicated student production crew and part-time staff, fostering professional development in sports media and production. Coordinate game-day staffing for home events, managing schedules, availability tracking, and all necessary staff communications. Partner with the Director of Competitive & Recreational Sports and the club sports coaching staff to implement and audit recruitment processes. Assist in establishing a robust data bank of prospects utilizing varied recruiting services, distributing prospect lists, and evaluating recruitment software efficiency. Lead the development of promotional graphics, target digital campaigns, and high-impact highlight videos to support coaches in attracting elite prospective student-athletes to RMU. Manage the setup, maintenance, and inventory of all digital streaming and production equipment, ensuring technical issues are proactively addressed. Serve as an additional point of contact to RMU Athletics and the Academic Media Center to streamline resource sharing and collaborate on university-wide video and audio content initiatives. Manage and optimize the Campus Recreation YouTube channel and secondary digital platforms. Track content analytics and implement tools to assess and improve online brand awareness. Assist with the maintenance of the Club Sports website, ensuring accurate and timely updates of team rosters, schedules, results, standings, news articles, recruiting information, multimedia content, and program announcements. Collaborate with coaches and team leadership to ensure all website content reflects current team operations and supports departmental marketing and recruitment objectives. Ensure all ACHA Men’s Division I ice hockey home games are live-streamed in compliance with league standards to facilitate scouting and public access. Support broader Campus Recreation and university initiatives, including representing Club Sports at admissions information sessions, open houses, and fundraising campaigns. Assist the Director of Competitive & Recreational Sports with daily administration and oversight of all Club Sport & Intramural programs, ensuring alignment with departmental, university, and governing body policies. Serve as a resource for club sport coaches, officers, and student leaders by guiding organizational management, policy interpretation, and program expectations. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned by the Director of Competitive & Recreational Sports, or other campus recreation administrators. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required—strongly preferred in Sport Management, Media Production, Sport Communication, Marketing, Graphic Design, or a closely related field. A combination of education and equivalent experience will also be considered. 3–5 years of progressive experience in video production, livestreaming, and digital marketing. Demonstrated experience in a leadership or supervisory capacity within a campus recreation, intercollegiate athletics, or club sports environment is highly preferred. Advanced proficiency in video production and live-broadcast software (e.g., Streamlabs, OBS, Adobe Premiere Pro) and graphic design applications (e.g., Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, Canva, or similar creative platforms). Exceptional organizational, communication, and project management skills. Proven ability to lead diverse teams, manage logistics under tight athletic schedules, and work independently with high strategic initiative. Exemption Status: Act 153 Clearance Required: Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): Yes Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 6, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498796/director-of-alumni-and-donor-engagement": {
      "title": "Director of Alumni and Donor Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Alumni and Donor Engagement Apply now Job no: 498796 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: University Advancement Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: The Director of Alumni and Donor Engagement is a key leader within University Advancement responsible for planning, executing, and measuring a comprehensive alumni engagement strategy while actively expanding donor stewardship and cultivation initiatives. This role builds meaningful connections with RMU alumni, strengthens the donor pipeline, and stewards positive relationships with top philanthropic prospects and contributors to advance the University’s mission. Responsibilities: Alumni Engagement & Volunteer Leadership: Lead the strategy, planning, and execution of all local, regional, and national alumni programming, including signature events (e.g., Homecoming Weekend, reunions, and affinity group gatherings). Establish and manage regional Alumni Network chapters, leading the identification of target regions, recruitment of network leaders, and management of local activities. Donor Engagement, Cultivation & Stewardship: Partner with the Executive Director to design, implement, and manage innovative donor recognition and stewardship programs aimed at retaining and elevating top prospects. Execute major prospect and donor events, including national tour stops, intimate cultivation gatherings, and specialized donor appreciation experiences. Collaborate closely with Leadership Gift Officers and the development team to identify alumni leadership prospects, map out pathways converting active alumni into donors, and integrate them into fundraising campaigns. Maintain strong partnerships across university units to ensure full compliance with donor intent and institutional policies. Strategic Communications & Marketing: Develop and execute integrated communication plans in collaboration with the Office of University Brand across the alumni website, social channels, e-newsletters, direct mail, and virtual platforms. Drive messaging that highlights volunteer opportunities, upcoming events, and student, university, and alumni/donor impact stories. Cross-Campus Collaboration: Partner with the Career Center and relevant departments to establish alumni mentorship programs for current students. Work with Admissions, Student Affairs, Academic Deans, and faculty to create targeted alumni interaction opportunities with legacy families, prospective students, and academic departments. Operations, Analytics & Supervision Establish, track, and evaluate quantitative engagement alumni metrics, based on CASE standards, to continuously optimize programs. Supervise, mentor, and evaluate student staff members. Oversee event budgets and perform operational duties as needed, including traveling or driving on behalf of the university when required. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree strongly preferred. 7+ years of progressive experience in higher education advancement, with a strong emphasis on alumni relations, donor engagement, and fundraising. Proven success in developing and implementing strategic plans for alumni engagement, including volunteer recruitment and management, event planning, and communications. Demonstrated experience in managing and supervising staff. Experience with donor databases (preferably Raiser’s Edge or a similar CRM) and fundraising software. Ability to develop and implement strategic plans for alumni engagement and donor relations that align with the institution’s overall mission and fundraising goals. Proven leadership and supervisory skills with the ability to motivate, mentor, and manage a high-performing team. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to build and maintain strong relationships with alumni, donors, faculty, staff, and other stakeholders. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including public speaking and presentation skills. Knowledge of fundraising principles and best practices, including donor segmentation, cultivation strategies, and stewardship plans. Ability to plan, organize, and execute successful alumni and donor events, volunteer programs, and other engagement initiatives. Ability to analyze data, track progress toward goals, and prepare reports on alumni engagement and fundraising activities. Proficiency with donor databases, CRM systems, and other relevant software applications. Experience with data analysis and reporting tools. Valid drivers license or the ability to have reliable transportation to travel on behalf of the university. Exemption Status: Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): Yes Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 5, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498794/guest-services-supervisor": {
      "title": "Guest Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Guest Services Supervisor Apply now Job no: 498794 Location: Island Sports Center Position Department: Guest Services Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: The Guest Services Supervisor is responsible for meeting and exceeding the needs of the customers at the Island Sports Center (ISC). The Guest Services Supervisor oversees a department that is the main contact point for guest relations and interactions. In addition, the Guest Services Supervisor provides departmental assistance to other ISC and university departments. Responsibilities: Performs general duties of Guest Services Associates, including: Greeting guests on site and attending to their needs. Providing enrollment programming services to guests and clients. Sending faxes, emails, sorting mail, and waivers. Assisting personnel of the sports center. Assisting with marketing, sales, and promotional activities Operating point-of-sale/cash register, handling cash/purchase transactions, and fulfilling ISC cash control policies. Oversee and assist Skate Guards. Oversees Guest Services staff to ensure they are meeting and exceeding customer needs, providing accurate programming and services information and assisting other ISC departments as needed. Manage Guest Services work schedule. Prepares and implements Guest Services Training. Assists with cash control policies as related to Guest Services. Coordinates communications to and from Guest Services. Responsible for recruiting, hiring, and mentoring of all Guest Services Associates and Skate Guards. Gain a thorough understanding of the Daysmart database. Oversee and audit the ISC Birthday Party program. Other duties as requested by the Assistant Director or Executive Director. Minimum Qualifications: High School education or equivalent required. Three (3) years of guest services supervisory experience preferred. Commitment to providing outstanding attention and service to Island Sports Center guests and clients. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Willingness to work various hours/shifts on weekdays, weekends, and/or holidays. Detail and accuracy oriented for record keeping and data entry. Ability to multi-task and work independently. Ability to run and balance a cash register. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: September 29, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
