    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498774/administrative-assistant": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant Apply now Job no: 498774 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Office of People and Culture Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: This position provides confidential administrative support to the Human Resources Department. This position also provides various administrative support to Business Affairs, Title IX. This position is supportive in all aspects of human resources including tracking of invoices, scheduling on-boarding, conducting onboarding for part-time employees. Assists with compliance projects and tracks certain benefits (tuition waiver). Maintains the HR website. Responsibilities: Manages, coordinates and arranges calendar and meeting arrangements on behalf of the departments. Maintains files and confidential records on behalf of the departments. Draft and provide input on correspondence and other communication on behalf of the departments. Manages projects as determined by the departments including projects with confidential and/or sensitive material. Prepare and reconcile various monthly invoices for Human Resources and Business Affairs. Manages coverage of the front desk in Human Resources and Human Resources inbox. Serves as the main point of contact for HR phone line and walk-ins and will triage to the appropriate HR colleague. Serves as initial point of contact for general benefits questions, life events, new hire benefits enrollment. Schedule campus wide cross functional meetings involving senior level leadership. Requests will be made at the request of the Vice President, Business Affairs, Chief Accounting and Financial Planning Officer, or the Vice President of People and Culture. Provide administrative support to Vice President, Business Affairs, Chief Accounting and Financial Planning Officer and the Vice President for People and Culture. Provides administrative support as needed for the Title IX office. Process employment verification requests. Eligible for a hybrid schedule, potentially one day a week work from home. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma required. Associates degree preferred. Minimum of three years of administrative assistant experience is required. Human Resources experience, leave management experience, employee benefits experience, wellness initiative experience is preferred. Ability to maintain a high degree of confidentiality. Proficient knowledge of computers including Microsoft Office packages including Word, Excel and PowerPoint and/or Google Docs. A willingness to develop computer skills and adjust to other updated technology. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to use discretion to make independent judgments, decisions and problem solve. Strong organizational skills; ability to prioritize multiple tasks and work with moderate supervision. Excellent customer relations and professional and interpersonal communication skills needed to interact closely with staff, faculty and students, deal with multiple constituencies and work with a diverse population. Ability to design presentations using presentation software such as PowerPoint, Google Slides or other presentation software. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: September 10, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498742/athletic-ticket-sales-and-service-account-representative": {
      "title": "Athletic Ticket Sales and Service Account Representative",
      "description": "Athletic Ticket Sales and Service Account Representative Apply now Job no: 498742 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: UPMC Events Center Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: RMU Athletics Ticket Sales and Service Account Representative position will learn and expand his/her knowledge of the fundamentals of the sales process through group sales, new season ticket sales and renewals across all ticketed sports. The Account Representative position will receive training, development and be provided the opportunity for rapid career advancement to Senior level sales roles, and leadership positions with added responsibility. Responsibilities: Sell a full menu of ticket products for all RMU ticketed Athletics events, via outbound phone calls and face- to-face presentations including, but not limited to, season tickets, flex ticket packages, group tickets, premium tickets, and premium hospitality packages. Must be able to work evenings and weekends, as required. All home games and other events hosted by RMU as assigned will be worked in various capacities: prospecting appointments, sales tables, and game events. Build relationships in the community and expand business with current ticket holders and cold call new prospects and referrals to drive revenue. Build out, plan, prospect and execute large scale group sales initiatives. Work in the assigned on campus location on a daily basis as well as go on in person meetings out in the community. Contact businesses in the local area via outbound phone calls, appointments and event-based selling. Deliver excellent customer service and cultivate relationships with current and future fans. Other related duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree with concentration in Sports Marketing or a related field is required 1+ Years experience in a sports selling role, college or professional. Experience working within Ticketmaster is preferred. Experience and success in an inside sales program or ticket sales role preferred. Comfort with making outbound phone calls in a professional and friendly manner. Strong work ethic, positive attitude and desire and ability to learn in a fast paced industry. Strong drive to learn the sales process and grow your career rapidly. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: September 2, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
