    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498755/administrative-coordinator-bayer-center-for-nonprofit-management-bcnm-and-the-covestro-center-for-community-engagement-ccec": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management (BCNM) and the Covestro Center for Community Engagement (CCEC)",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management (BCNM) and the Covestro Center for Community Engagement (CCEC) Apply now Job no: 498755 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management and Covestro Center for Community Engagement Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: The Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to the Bayer Center for Nonprofit Management (BCNM) and the Covestro Center for Community Engagement (CCCE). This role requires exceptional organizational skills, technology skills, attention to detail, proactive problem-solving abilities, and the capacity to manage diverse tasks efficiently in a fast-paced environment. The Administrative Assistant will serve as a key point of contact, manage schedules and communications, and support the smooth functioning of both Centers activities and programs. Responsibilities: Administrative Support: Manage scheduling meetings, appointments, special events, programming and travel arrangements for Directors and Chief Officer. Prepare agendas, take minutes, and follow up on action items for meetings. Organize and maintain electronic and physical filing systems, ensuring information is easily accessible. Prepare correspondence, reports, presentations, and other documents as needed. Handle incoming and outgoing mail, email, and phone communications, prioritizing and directing appropriately. Assist with office management tasks, such as ordering supplies and coordinating equipment maintenance. Maintain and update contact lists and databases. Programmatic Support (Bayer Center): Assist with the coordination of educational programs, including scheduling logistics, preparing materials, and managing registrations. Support the preparation and distribution of consulting reports and other client-related documents. Assist with the administrative aspects of the Wage and Benefit survey, such as data entry and distribution. Help coordinate communication with instructors and consultants. Programmatic Support (Covestro Center): Provide administrative support for the BoardsWork!, Executive Service Corps, and SkillShare programs. Assist with the preparation of training materials, surveys, forms, and agreements. Help coordinate logistics for program events, workshops, and kick-off/ending celebrations. Assist with the collection and organization of program evaluation data. Support the maintenance of business and nonprofit contracts related to CCCE programs. Data Management and Financial Assistance: Assist with data entry into Salesforce or other relevant databases. Help track Institute revenue opportunities, contacts, projects, and reports. Assist with the administrative aspects of revenue management such as organizing documentation and tracking reporting deadlines. Process expense reports and invoices, as needed. Marketing and Communications Support: Assist with the preparation and distribution of marketing materials, including social media posts, website content updates, and brochures. Help collect information and stories related to the impact of the both Centers. Assist with the coordination of special events related to both centers. General Support: Serve as a point of contact for inquiries related to the ICenters, providing information and directing individuals appropriately. Maintain confidentiality of sensitive information. Exercise discretion and good judgment in handling administrative matters. Provide support for special projects as assigned by Directors and Chief Officer. Collaborate effectively with other university staff, volunteers, and external partners. Perform other duties as assigned to ensure the efficient operation of both Centers and to support the Collaborative Learning Institute (CLI) in general. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required; Associate's or Bachelor's degree preferred. Proven experience (typically 3+ years) as an administrative assistant, preferably supporting a senior-level manager or multiple programs. Exceptional organizational and time management skills with the ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) and other relevant software. Experience with database management (e.g., Salesforce) is a plus. Experience with Project Management software is a plus. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Proactive and resourceful problem-solving skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: August 28, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498756/administrative-coordinator-collaborative-learning-institute-cli": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator:  Collaborative Learning Institute (CLI)",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator: Collaborative Learning Institute (CLI) Apply now Job no: 498756 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Collaborative Learning Institute Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: The Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for the Collaborative Learning Institute (CLI). This position serves as a primary point of contact for students, visitors, faculty, staff, employers, vendors, and community partners while helping to ensure that CLI’s daily operations, facilities, events, contracts, invoicing, and administrative processes are organized and running smoothly. The Administrative Coordinator maintains a welcoming and professional environment for students and visitors and works closely with CLI Leadership and university departments to coordinate the logistical and administrative needs of the Institute. The position requires strong organization, attention to detail, follow-through, customer service, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced learning and event environment. Responsibilities: Front Desk & Reception ● Serve as a primary point of contact for students, visitors, faculty, staff, employers, community members, and other guests entering the Institute. ● Greet students and visitors in a warm, welcoming, and professional manner. ● Provide basic information regarding CLI programs, schedules, events, facilities, and office procedures. ● Direct students, visitors, and guests to the appropriate staff member, classroom, meeting space, or campus resource. ● Monitor the reception area and ensure visitors receive timely assistance. ● Answer and respond to general inquiries and direct questions to the appropriate CLI staff member or university department. Office & Facilities Coordination ● Coordinate day-to-day office operations and administrative needs for CLI. ● Monitor office supplies and maintain adequate inventory of paper, office supplies, water, and other commonly used materials. ● Order and restock supplies as needed or as requested by CLI Leadership. ● Receive, sort, and distribute mail and deliveries. ● Maintain and organize CLI’s two designated storage areas. ● Coordinate with Colonial Central, Information Technology (IT), and other university departments as needed. ● Maintain the CLI classroom, conference room, reception area, and other designated spaces on a daily basis. ● Ensure CLI spaces are appropriately prepared and maintained for meetings, classes, and events. ● Assist with the preparation and organization of materials and spaces to support the daily operation of the Institute. Contracts & Agreement Support ● Create and enter contracts and agreements into Workday as directed by CLI Leadership. ● Maintain the CLI tracking spreadsheet for agreements and contracts. ● Monitor agreement information and maintain accurate and up-to-date records. ● Support CLI Leadership with administrative follow-up related to contracts and agreements. Tuition Discount Agreement Support ● Monitor tuition discount agreements and notify CLI Leadership of upcoming renewals and required action. ● Provide necessary contact information and documentation related to tuition discount agreements prior to renewal. ● Complete and coordinate required updates for Edcor/FedEx as required by the Tuition Discount Agreement (TDA) process. ● Maintain accurate records related to tuition discount agreements and renewals. Invoicing & Financial Administrative Support ● Create invoices as directed by CLI Leadership. ● Monitor invoice and payment activity and notify appropriate RMU staff when payments are received or past due. ● Complete required control sheets and deliver checks to Student Financial Services. ● Maintain CLI accounts within Touchnet, excluding Career Fair transactions. ● Assist CLI Leadership with routine financial and administrative processes as assigned. ● Maintain accurate documentation and records related to CLI invoicing and payments. Event Coordination & Support ● Coordinate the administrative and logistical needs of CLI events as directed by CLI Leadership. ● Maintain the CLI event calendar and ensure scheduled events are accurately reflected. ● Coordinate with the UPMC Events Center, as needed, to arrange facilities, room setups, logistics, and other event requirements. ● Work with Parkhurst and outside vendors to coordinate food and catering for CLI events. ● Communicate event requirements and logistical details to appropriate university departments, vendors, employers, and other partners. ● Ensure classrooms, conference rooms, and event spaces are set up according to specifications provided by CLI Leadership and employers. ● Prepare and organize learning materials, name tents, posters, directional signage, handouts, and other event materials. ●Attend corporate training events with professional dress and work as a liaison for training participants and the CLI ● Ensure required materials are printed, organized, and placed appropriately prior to events. ● Assist with on-site event logistics and address routine administrative or logistical needs as they arise. ● Ensure event spaces are returned to an appropriate condition following events. Other ● Support with Handshake - event and job approvals ● Perform other administrative duties and special projects as assigned in support of the Collaborative Learning Institute. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required; Associate's or Bachelor's degree preferred. Proven experience (typically 3+ years) as an administrative assistant, preferably supporting a senior-level manager or multiple programs. Exceptional organizational and time management skills with the ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail and accuracy. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) and other relevant software. Experience with database management (e.g., Salesforce) is a plus. Experience with Project Management software is a plus. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Proactive and resourceful problem-solving skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: August 28, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498758/assistant-director-strategic-communications": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Strategic Communications",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Strategic Communications Apply now Job no: 498758 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Athletics Media Relations Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: The Assistant Director, Strategic Communications assists with the creation and implementation of overall design strategy across all aspects of the athletic department and is responsible for oversight of all media relations functions for assigned sports, within the guidelines, rules, and regulations of the University and NCAA. Responsibilities: Disseminates information for all assigned sports. Writes, edits, and distributes sports information, including Athletic Department website stories, social media content, press releases, team record books, and media interviews, on a timely basis. Compiles and reports statistical information, competition records, and archival information on a timely basis. Responds to University and public inquiries related to athletic events, student-athletes, and coaches. Coordinates and promotes the nomination of outstanding student-athletes as candidates for Conference, Regional, and National awards, both athletic and academic. Provides media relations coverage on the day of competition. Assists with the development of copy and design for marketing and communication pieces, including athletic publications, press releases, social media, and content for the athletics app and website, to increase brand awareness and expand visibility for RMU Athletics. Assists with the design of digital and print materials, including graphics creation through Adobe Photoshop. Serves as liaison to the Student-Athlete Advisory Committee to support production and distribution of marketing and communication materials for student development initiatives. Maintains assigned sport workflows and task tracking in Asana. Represents RMU Athletics professionally at all times, including in public and social media conduct, as a representative of the University. Must be available by phone and email after typical business hours. Other duties and responsibilities as assigned, including serving as Game Management administrator for selected events. Assists in hiring game-day workers for home competitions of assigned sports, including statisticians, clock operators, public address announcers, and scorekeepers, and provides supervision of game-day workers during home competition. Provides statistical and/or game-tracking services during athletic competition as needed for assigned sports. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree preferred. Minimum two years experience in collegiate media relations. Strong writing skills, communication skills, and organizational skills. Proficient in social media platforms and website development. Knowledge of and commitment to all University and NCAA rules. Competency in Adobe Photoshop, experience in Adobe Premiere and/or After Effects Exemption Status: Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): Yes Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: August 28, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
