    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498826/coordinator-of-corporate-donor-community-relations-and-events": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Corporate, Donor, Community Relations and Events",
      "description": "Coordinator of Corporate, Donor, Community Relations and Events Apply now Job no: 498826 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Athletics Administration Position Type: Staff Part-Time Overview: The Coordinator of Corporate, Donor, Community Relations and Events position supports RMU Athletics in raising, stewarding, and growing private and corporate support for Colonial student-athletes. The role cultivates and stewards donors, services corporate partners, plans and executes department events, and builds lasting ties between RMU Athletics and the Pittsburgh community. This position is a front line ambassador for the department and helps convert community goodwill into sustained investment in student-athlete success. Responsibilities: Fundraising (approximately 30%) * Manage an assigned portfolio of annual fund donors and prospects, with a focus on acquisition, renewal, and upgrades. * Support annual giving campaigns, including Day of Giving, sport specific recurring giving campaigns, and Varsity Club appeals. * Conduct cultivation and solicitation visits, calls, and outreach in partnership with Madeline Menzie and development staff. * Use department events as cultivation and solicitation opportunities with key donors and prospects. * Track all contacts, gifts, and pledges in the university donor database and report progress toward goals. Donor Stewardship (approximately 20%) * Develop and carry out a stewardship plan that thanks, recognizes, and reports impact to donors at every giving level. * Coordinate timely gift acknowledgments, impact reports, and personal touch points from coaches and student-athletes. * Plan donor recognition opportunities, including game day hospitality, behind the scenes experiences, and recognition listings. * Partner with student-athletes and SAAC on thank you initiatives that connect donors to the people they support. Corporate Partnerships (approximately 15%) * Identify and cultivate local and regional businesses for sponsorship and partnership opportunities. * Service existing corporate partners, ensuring contractual benefits such as signage, hospitality, and promotions are delivered and documented. * Prepare proposals, partner recaps, and renewal materials in coordination with the department's multimedia rights holder, as applicable. Community Relations (approximately 15%) * Coordinate student-athlete community service, school visits, youth clinics, and appearances. * Build relationships with civic organizations, chambers of commerce, schools, and alumni groups in the Pittsburgh region. * Represent RMU Athletics at community events and identify outreach that drives attendance, engagement, and giving. * Track and report community engagement hours and outcomes. Events (approximately 20%) * Plan and execute signature athletics events, including golf outings, Tip Off, donor receptions, and community nights. * Manage event logistics, including budgets, timelines, venues, vendors, catering, invitations, and RSVPs. * Coordinate game day hospitality and premium experiences for donors and corporate partners. * Recruit and manage event volunteers and student-athlete participation. * Conduct post event evaluations, tracking attendance, revenue, and follow up actions. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in sport management, marketing, communications, nonprofit management, business, or a related field. At least one year of experience in fundraising, sales, sponsorship, donor relations, or community outreach, which may include internships or graduate assistantships. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with comfort speaking to donors, business leaders, and community groups. Organized and detail oriented, able to manage multiple projects, events, and deadlines. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and home athletic events as needed. Commitment to a student-athlete centered approach and to representing RMU with integrity. Exemption Status: Non-Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): Yes Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 23, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498808/programmer-analyst": {
      "title": "Programmer Analyst",
      "description": "Programmer Analyst Apply now Job no: 498808 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Enterprise Applications Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: The Programmer - Analyst role is an integral part of the IT Applications team supporting new and existing software solutions used across the University; a junior to mid-tier role depending on experience level. This role consists primarily of software development and related analysis/analyst activities. Two or more years of SQL development experience is required (Oracle SQL and/or PostgreSQL) possessing intermediate / advanced SQL skills along with software development experience / exposure using the C# programming language. Experience working with Oracle or PostgreSQL relational databases is required and experience developing extract, transform, load (ETL) data integration processes, utilizing vendor APIs and working with cloud/SaaS software solutions is strongly desired. Experience with the Ellucian higher education product suite including Banner, Ethos, Insights, Data Connect and Business Process Automation (workflow) is strongly desired. If working as part of a small, high-performing team, in a fast-paced environment, where you will learn and make a difference is appealing, this opportunity may be the right fit! Robert Morris University offers great benefits including tuition reimbursement and with this role, the opportunity to work in a hybrid capacity (remote / on campus as needed). Candidates must be able to commute to the Moon Township, PA campus as needed per work requirements. Responsibilities: Provides application development and IT analysis services. This scope includes learning and supporting various 3rd party applications. Develops requirements and specifications for new software applications and analyzes change requests for existing applications. Translates requirements into technical solutions. Creates / maintains documentation for existing applications and processes. Collaborates closely with internal customers throughout the University to identify and document project requirements, specifications and priority. Participates in and/or leads business process mapping and gap analysis activities. Collaborates with vendors as needed. Responsible for functional verification and testing activities (test plan creation and execution); ensuring that the developed software applications meet customer requirements based on the specifications, ensuring minimal defects. Accountable for identification and documentation of risks, defects, and issues throughout the project lifecycle. Responsible for assisting in the resolution of risks, defects, and issues. May be accountable for a project schedule / deliverables. Responsible for providing proactive project feedback to IT management and/or internal customers. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Science or a related field. 2+ years experience as a software developer/analyst. Intermediate / advanced Oracle SQL and/or PostgreSQL skills are required. Intermediate / advanced experience working with Oracle and/or PostgreSQL relational databases is also required. Oracle PL/SQL experience is a plus and the ideal candidate will also have C# software development experience. Experience with the Ellucian higher education product suite including Banner, Ethos, Insights, Data Connect and Business Process Automation (workflow) is strongly desired. Experience developing extract, transform, load (ETL) data integration processes, utilizing vendor APIs and working with cloud/SaaS software solutions is strongly desired. The ability and desire to learn new technology is required. The ability to work in a self-directed manner as well as part of a team is required; delivering assignments as scheduled. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills are required. Strong interpersonal and customer service skills are required. Strong organizational skills and flexibility to work in a performance driven, multi-tasking environment are required. Experience working with sensitive/confidential information (ex.FERPA) is a plus. Experience with / knowledge of secure IT coding / data transfer techniques (ex. use of encryption) is a plus. Exemption Status: Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 20, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498811/rooney-international-visiting-scholar": {
      "title": "Rooney International Visiting Scholar",
      "description": "Rooney International Visiting Scholar Apply now Job no: 498811 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Center for Global Engagement Position School: Administration: No School Overview: OPPORTUNITY The Rooney International Visiting Scholar Program offers international scholars the opportunity to spend a semester in residence at Robert Morris University pursuing research, and/ or teaching while interacting with faculty, staff, and students. The Rooney Scholars live on campus in the Rooney House and become part of the campus community. Travel expenses will be provided and well as an automobile for the Scholar’s use (valid driver’s license required). A salary is provided. RMU is currently accepting applications for the Academic Year 2026-27, for Spring 2027 (approximately, January 15-May 7, 2027). Priority Consideration will be given to applications received by: October 23, 2026 for Spring 2027 residence. Responsibilities: During their semester residency at RMU, Rooney Scholars may participate in a variety of activities, such as: Pursuing independent research objectives and collaborating with faculty, staff, or/and students on research projects. Delivering formal presentations to the university community or/and to specific academic schools. Presenting guest lectures in classes. Teaching a course within their host school. Preference is given to applicants who include a plan to work with RMU faculty on joint research projects. Minimum Qualifications: The applicant will have a Ph.D. or an advanced degree in a related discipline offered at Robert Morris University, or significant experience in an area of cultural or humanitarian interest to the University. A list of RMU Schools and programs of study can be found here: RMU Programs Applicants should have a distinguished academic and/or professional record, and must be committed to excellence in teaching and learning. Applicants must also demonstrate leadership skills, communications skills in English, as well as the ability to work collaboratively with others in an academic environment. Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check: Yes Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Advertised: October 20, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498820/financial-aid-counselor": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor Apply now Job no: 498820 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Financial Aid Counseling Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: Will have extensive knowledge of federal, state and institutional student aid regulations and procedures, and be able to effectively communicate that information to students and parents. This position is primarily in-office, however, remote flexibilities are offered occasionally, per manager's approval. Responsibilities: Manages the financial aid process for approximately one-third (1/3) of the student population which includes freshmen, transfer, continuing undergraduate, graduate, doctorate, online, off campus and certificate programs. Counsels students and parents on financial aid policies and procedures through personal appointments, walk-ins, phone calls and emailed messages. Adheres to and communicates federal, state and institutional policy information. Emphasis on strong customer service practices. Presents various payment and financing options. Recommends ways to reduce loan debt. Responsible for completing verification and monitoring of student files. Requests necessary documents required for file completion. Reviews household and income data through review of federal tax returns, W-2s, and other relevant income documentation, and reports corrections to Department of Education when necessary. Thorough understanding of federal tax code to ensure accuracy of review process. Rectify non valid FAFSAs, which may include review of citizenship documentation, loan borrowing history, previous enrollment, social security administration database mismatches, veteran status, selective service registration, drug convictions, marital status discrepancies, dependency status issues and other conflicting information. Recommends, collects and reviews all relevant documentation concerning dependency override and professional judgement scenarios. Promptly returns phone calls and emails to prospective and currents students and parents. Represents the University at on-campus and off-campus programs, including orientations, Life Skills, financial aid nights and college fairs. Staffs a financial aid booth and answers financial aid related questions. Face to face meetings discussing specific financial aid questions. Presentation of financial aid information in a group setting. Keeps current on regulatory updates by attending training sessions and workshops and by maintaining membership in PASFAA and NASFAA. All other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree is preferred or equivalent work experience. 2+ years of financial aid experience is preferred. Ability to work with and maintain confidential student and University information. Extensive knowledge of federal and state financial aid policies. Excellent written and verbal communications skills. Strong commitment to customer service. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. On occasion may need to work evening and/or weekend hours. Exemption Status: Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: No Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 20, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498823/head-coach-mens-wrestling": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Men's Wrestling",
      "description": "Head Coach, Men's Wrestling Apply now Job no: 498823 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Men's Wrestling Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: Serve as the founding head coach of Robert Morris University's NCAA Division I Men's Wrestling program. Responsible for student-athlete welfare and for building, managing, operating, fundraising for and administering the program within the guidelines, rules and regulations of Robert Morris University, [conference affiliation] and the NCAA. This includes recruiting the inaugural roster, awarding athletic scholarships, establishing the competition schedule and program operations, and creating a culture built on academic achievement, competitive excellence and personal development. Responsibilities: Build the inaugural NCAA Division I Men's Wrestling program, including recruiting the first roster, developing the competition schedule, establishing practice room, equipment and facility needs, and setting team policies and program standards in partnership with athletics administration. Use expert technical knowledge of wrestling to develop and coach a successful program, including teaching technique, strategy and match tactics, organizing and supervising practice, conditioning and workouts, overseeing home events, managing travel for away events, and supervising staff. Establish a leadership and mentor role among student-athletes, assistant coaches and support staff while promoting sportsmanship and responsible behavior during and outside of competition. Assist with the preparation and control of, and operate within, the budget established for the sport, including athletic scholarship allocations. Manage equipment, uniform and apparel inventory and purchasing using the University purchasing card in accordance with University policy. Scout and recruit quality student-athletes from geographically and demographically diverse populations who fit the academic and athletic profile of the University. Coordinate admissions with athletics compliance and the Office of Admissions. Arrange and oversee all campus visits and travel itineraries, and supervise all correspondence with prospects, coaches, parents and alumni. Operate youth camps and clinics in accordance with University policies on the protection of minors. Encourage and promote academic excellence and retention. Work with athletic academic advising staff on study hall, monitoring of individual academic performance, eligibility and graduation progress, and referral to appropriate University resources. Perform public relations and community engagement with faculty, students, parents, donors, alumni and University administrators. Build relationships with the regional high school, club and youth wrestling community and with state and national wrestling organizations. Work with the Men's Wrestling Advisory Board and lead program fundraising efforts in partnership with athletics development. Work closely with sports medicine and athletic training staff to ensure the safety and health of student-athletes, including adherence to the NCAA wrestling weight management program and skin infection protocols. Establish, communicate and enforce RMU, Athletic Department and team regulations regarding student conduct, appearance and behavior. Maintain knowledge of and commitment to all NCAA, conference and University regulations, policies and procedures. Report any known or suspected NCAA violations to athletics compliance, the Director of Athletics or the Faculty Athletics Representative. Violation of NCAA regulations shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective action up to and including termination of employment. Complete required compliance paperwork in a timely fashion. Perform miscellaneous duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree preferred. At least five years of wrestling coaching experience at the collegiate level required. NCAA Division I coaching experience, experience building or rebuilding a program, and collegiate competitive experience preferred. Strong leadership, communication and organizational skills. Established recruiting relationships in the wrestling community. Knowledge of and commitment to student-athlete welfare, weight management, academic success and NCAA and University rules. Demonstrated ability to engage donors and the community. Ability to work nights and weekends. Valid driver's license required. Current CPR, AED and First Aid certification required, or the ability to obtain within 30 days of hire. Exemption Status: Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): Yes Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 19, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/856/cw/en-us/job/498824/head-coach-womens-flag-football": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Women's Flag Football",
      "description": "Head Coach, Women's Flag Football Apply now Job no: 498824 Location: Moon Campus Position Department: Women's Flag Football Position Type: Staff Full-Time Overview: Serve as the founding head coach of Robert Morris University's intercollegiate Women's Flag Football program. Responsible for student-athlete welfare and for building, managing, operating, fundraising for and administering the program within the guidelines, rules and regulations of Robert Morris University, [conference or governing body affiliation] and the NCAA. This includes recruiting the inaugural roster, establishing the competition schedule and program operations, and creating a culture built on academic achievement, competitive excellence and personal development. Responsibilities: Build the inaugural Women's Flag Football program, including recruiting the first roster, developing the competition schedule, establishing equipment, facility and practice needs, and setting team policies and program standards in partnership with athletics administration. Use expert technical knowledge of flag football to develop and coach a successful program, including developing high quality student-athletes, organizing and supervising practice, conditioning and workouts, overseeing home events, managing travel for away events, and supervising staff. Establish a leadership and mentor role among student-athletes, assistant coaches and support staff while promoting sportsmanship and responsible behavior during and outside of competition. Assist with the preparation and control of, and operate within, the budget established for the sport. Manage equipment inventory and purchasing using the University purchasing card in accordance with University policy. Scout and recruit quality student-athletes from geographically and demographically diverse populations to meet roster goals. Coordinate admissions with athletics compliance and the Office of Admissions. Arrange and oversee all campus visits and travel itineraries, and supervise all correspondence with prospects, coaches, parents and alumni. Operate youth camps and clinics in accordance with University policies on the protection of minors. Encourage and promote academic excellence. Work with athletic academic advising staff on study hall, monitoring of individual academic performance and personal development, and referral to appropriate University resources. Perform public relations and community engagement with faculty, students, parents, donors, alumni and University administrators. Promote the sport at the local, state and national level, including high school and youth flag football growth in the region. Lead program fundraising efforts in partnership with athletics development. Work closely with sports medicine and athletic training staff to ensure the safety and health of student-athletes. Establish, communicate and enforce RMU, Athletic Department and team regulations regarding student conduct, appearance and behavior. Maintain knowledge of and commitment to all NCAA, conference and University regulations, policies and procedures. Report any known or suspected NCAA violations to athletics compliance, the Director of Athletics or the Faculty Athletics Representative. Violation of NCAA regulations shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective action up to and including termination of employment. Complete required compliance paperwork in a timely fashion. Perform miscellaneous duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree preferred. At least three years of coaching experience in flag football or football at the collegiate, high school or club level required. Experience coaching women's flag football and experience building or growing a program preferred. Strong communication, organizational and interpersonal skills. Ability to recruit and build a roster from the ground up. Knowledge of and commitment to student-athlete welfare, academic success and NCAA and University rules. Demonstrated ability to engage donors and the community. Valid driver's license required. Current CPR, AED and First Aid certification required, or the ability to obtain within 30 days of hire. Exemption Status: Exempt Act 153 Clearance Required: Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): Yes Required to Pass a Credit Check: Yes Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: October 19, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    }
